---
import { BaseLayout } from "@walle/layouts";
import { SectionHeaderStandard } from "@walle/components";

const lastUpdated = "August 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  headerTitle="Privacy Policy"
  headerDescription="How italiaopensource.com handles personal data."
  headerRobots="noindex, follow"
>
  <SectionHeaderStandard
    title="Privacy Policy"
    subtitle="What italiaopensource.com collects, and what it doesn't."
    variant="secondary"
  />

  <article class="legal">
    <p class="legal__meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <h2>1. Overview</h2>
    <p>
      italiaopensource.com is a static, community-maintained directory published by Italia
      Open-Source. It lists open-source projects, tech communities and partners, all sourced from
      the public
      <a href="https://github.com/italia-opensource/awesome-italia-opensource" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >awesome-italia-opensource</a
      > repository. The site does not have user accounts and does not run any tracking script of its
      own.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Hosting logs</strong>: the site is served by GitHub Pages, which may log standard
        request data (IP address, browser, referrer) under
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >GitHub's own privacy statement</a
        >. We don't have access to this data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Content you submit</strong>: adding or updating a project or community happens via a
        pull request on GitHub, and applying as a Community Partner happens via a Google Form. Both
        are handled directly by GitHub and Google under their own privacy terms, not by us.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This site does not set any cookies of its own. If we ever enable analytics, this page will be
      updated first and a cookie notice will be shown.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>The site links out to, and relies on, the following third parties:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://pages.github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Pages</a> for hosting
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/italia-opensource" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> for the
        open-source data, contributions and pull requests
      </li>
      <li><a href="https://forms.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Forms</a> for partner applications</li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/italia-open-source" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >LinkedIn</a
        > for our company page
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Since we don't collect or store personal data ourselves, most requests (access, correction,
      deletion) need to go to the service that actually holds it: GitHub or Google. For anything
      related to a listing on this site, reach out via
      <a href="https://github.com/italia-opensource/awesome-italia-opensource/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >GitHub Issues</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Changes</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated as the site evolves. Material changes will be reflected here with a new "last updated" date.</p>

    <h2>7. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy can be sent via
      <a href="https://github.com/italia-opensource/awesome-italia-opensource/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >GitHub Issues</a
      > or through our
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/italia-open-source" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-3xl) var(--space-xl) var(--space-4xl);
  }

  .legal__meta {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .legal ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .legal li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }
</style>
